 `docs/lifecycle-plan.md` contains the frozen scope/search prompt, upgrade identities, acceptance and next public-release maintenance trigger. `.ai/README.md` routes current app facts. Git tags preserve pristine, baseline, changed and upgraded checkpoints. The framework repository retains the portable bundle/report; this application's context is never replaced from a newer skeleton.
+
+The immutable Alpha 7 framework archive contains preparation-time README/setup wording that still calls Alpha 6 current. For this retained application, use the committed lock and the exact references in the frozen lifecycle plan; do not downgrade because of that snapshot. Current-source evaluation is a separate pinned checkpoint, never evidence of a newly published release. Maintainer example paths in installed guides refer to the source repository at the locked framework revision; they are deliberately absent from the Composer archive.
